 "hook": {
  "text": "WHAT IS THIS\nDOING IN IRAQ?",
  "until": 2.6,
  "y": 0.12,
  "size": 110,
  "accent": [
   "IRAQ?"
  ]
 },
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "This tiny stone was dug up in Iraq.",
   "emph": [
    "iraq."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "But it wasn't made there.",
   "emph": [
    "wasn't"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "It's an Indus seal... carved more than two thousand kilometres away.",
   "caption": "It's an Indus seal... carved more than 2,000 kilometres away.",
   "emph": [
    "indus",
    "2,000"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "So how did it get there?",
   "emph": [
    "how"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Ships. Around twenty-three hundred BC, King Sargon of Akkad wrote that ships from a land called Meluhha docked at his capital.",
   "caption": "Ships. Around 2300 BC, King Sargon of Akkad wrote that ships from a land called Meluhha docked at his capital.",
   "emph": [
    "ships.",
    "meluhha"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "They brought bright red carnelian, and precious wood.",
   "emph": [
    "carnelian,"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Many historians believe Meluhha... was the Indus Valley.",
   "emph": [
    "indus",
    "valley."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "In the royal tombs of Ur, the elite were buried with red beads, drilled the Indus way.",
   "emph": [
    "royal",
    "indus"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Then, archaeologists found a seal that changes everything.",
   "emph": [
    "everything."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "It belonged to a man named Shuilishu.",
   "caption": "It belonged to a man named Shu-ilishu.",
   "emph": []
  },
  {
   "text": "Carved beside him, his job: interpreter of the Meluhhan language.",
   "emph": [
    "interpreter"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Over four thousand years ago, someone in Iraq could talk with the Indus people.",
   "caption": "Over 4,000 years ago, someone in Iraq could talk with the Indus people.",
   "emph": [
    "4,000",
    "talk"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "He understood them.",
   "emph": [
    "understood"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Today... no one can read a word they wrote.",
   "emph": [
    "read"
   ]
  }
 ],
